1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,470
In March 2012, Forbes ranked a
Brazilian 7th among the richest

2
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:08,140
people on the planet: $30 billion.

3
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:14,496
Two and a half years later, that
same man told the newspaper

4
00:00:14,496 --> 00:00:18,590
Folha de S.Paulo that his net
worth was negative: minus $1

5
00:00:18,590 --> 00:00:19,155
billion.

6
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:23,210
That's not a typo. Yes, minus.

7
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:27,951
This is the story of Eike Batista.
The man who put an X in the

8
00:00:27,951 --> 00:00:32,203
names of his companies because, to
him, the X meant multiply.

9
00:00:32,203 --> 00:00:36,315
And how, in the end, what
multiplied the most was the debt.

10
00:00:38,835 --> 00:00:41,070
Chapter 1. The mining heir.

11
00:00:42,845 --> 00:00:48,423
Eike Fuhrken Batista was born on
November 3, 1956, in Governador

12
00:00:48,423 --> 00:00:50,515
Valadares, Minas Gerais.

13
00:00:51,770 --> 00:00:55,920
His father, Eliezer Batista, was
one of the most powerful names

14
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,938
in Brazilian mining: he ran the
mining giant Vale do Rio Doce

15
00:00:59,938 --> 00:01:02,770
and served as Minister of Mines
and Energy.

16
00:01:03,190 --> 00:01:07,060
His mother, Jutta, was German. And
it was to Germany that young

17
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:10,931
Eike went to study metallurgical
engineering, at the University

18
00:01:10,931 --> 00:01:11,545
of Aachen.

19
00:01:13,010 --> 00:01:14,575
He never finished the degree.

20
00:01:15,630 --> 00:01:19,776
In the early 1980s, he returned to
Brazil with an idea: get into

21
00:01:19,776 --> 00:01:23,275
the Amazon gold trade, in the
middle of the gold rush.

22
00:01:24,523 --> 00:01:28,536
According to accounts from the
time, he borrowed $500,000 from

23
00:01:28,536 --> 00:01:32,678
jeweler friends to start buying
gold in the region and reselling

24
00:01:32,678 --> 00:01:33,973
it in the Southeast.

25
00:01:34,688 --> 00:01:39,425
By Eike's own account, in about a
year and a half the business

26
00:01:39,425 --> 00:01:40,648
made $6 million.

27
00:01:41,068 --> 00:01:43,188
He wasn't even 30 yet.

28
00:01:44,888 --> 00:01:48,108
Chapter 2. The headline-making
millionaire.

29
00:01:49,153 --> 00:01:52,520
In the following years, Eike moved
from trading to gold mining

30
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:54,963
and became a well-known figure in
the market.

31
00:01:56,233 --> 00:01:59,273
But his real fame came from
outside the business world.

32
00:01:59,693 --> 00:02:03,778
In 1990, according to the press at
the time, he became world

33
00:02:03,778 --> 00:02:08,068
champion in offshore powerboat
racing, high-speed boat races on

34
00:02:08,068 --> 00:02:08,953
the open sea.

35
00:02:09,723 --> 00:02:14,214
In 1991, he married Luma de
Oliveira, one of the most famous

36
00:02:14,214 --> 00:02:18,779
women in the country. They stayed
together until 2004 and had

37
00:02:18,779 --> 00:02:19,453
two sons.

38
00:02:21,038 --> 00:02:25,046
Eike never hid his taste for
luxury. Years later, he even kept

39
00:02:25,046 --> 00:02:29,055
cars like a Lamborghini Aventador
on display inside his living

40
00:02:29,055 --> 00:02:29,378
room.

41
00:02:31,103 --> 00:02:33,953
But the big leap was still to
come.

42
00:02:35,098 --> 00:02:37,608
Chapter 3. The X empire.

43
00:02:38,803 --> 00:02:42,752
In the second half of the 2000s,
Brazil was riding a wave of

44
00:02:42,752 --> 00:02:46,963
euphoria. The economy was growing,
foreign money was pouring in,

45
00:02:46,963 --> 00:02:50,583
and everyone was talking about the
pre-salt oil fields.

46
00:02:51,003 --> 00:02:53,763
Eike read the mood before anyone
else.

47
00:02:54,183 --> 00:02:58,156
He built the EBX group, with his
own initials in the name, and

48
00:02:58,156 --> 00:03:01,103
started launching companies one
after another.

49
00:03:01,523 --> 00:03:08,167
MMX, in mining. MPX, in energy.
LLX, in logistics. OSX, in

50
00:03:08,167 --> 00:03:14,468
shipbuilding. And the crown jewel:
OGX, in oil and gas.

51
00:03:16,513 --> 00:03:20,557
All of them with the X. According
to Eike himself, the letter

52
00:03:20,557 --> 00:03:23,143
stood for the multiplication of
wealth.

53
00:03:23,563 --> 00:03:28,255
OGX was founded in 2007 and, at
the end of that year, won oil

54
00:03:28,255 --> 00:03:33,178
exploration blocks in an auction
held by Brazil's oil regulator,

55
00:03:33,178 --> 00:03:33,793
the ANP.

56
00:03:34,213 --> 00:03:38,624
In June 2008, it debuted on the
stock exchange and raised 6.7

57
00:03:38,624 --> 00:03:42,891
billion reais. It was the largest
IPO in the history of the

58
00:03:42,891 --> 00:03:45,928
Brazilian stock exchange up to
that point.

59
00:03:46,348 --> 00:03:49,673
More than 60% of that money came
from foreign investors.

60
00:03:51,225 --> 00:03:55,710
And here's the most striking
detail: when it went public, OGX

61
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:58,945
had not yet produced a single
barrel of oil.

62
00:04:00,208 --> 00:04:04,090
Whoever bought the stock was
buying a promise. The promise that

63
00:04:04,090 --> 00:04:07,048
there was a lot of oil at the
bottom of the sea.

64
00:04:07,468 --> 00:04:14,818
And the market believed it. On
October 15, 2010, OGX stock hit

65
00:04:14,818 --> 00:04:18,493
its all-time high: 23.27 reais.

66
00:04:19,851 --> 00:04:22,016
Chapter 4. The peak.

67
00:04:23,026 --> 00:04:27,009
In 2011, Eike said publicly that
he would overtake the richest

68
00:04:27,009 --> 00:04:31,056
man in the world, Mexico's Carlos
Slim. And he said he had sent

69
00:04:31,056 --> 00:04:34,975
Slim a message: Slim had better
keep an eye on both rear-view

70
00:04:34,975 --> 00:04:38,958
mirrors, because Eike didn't know
which side he would pass him

71
00:04:38,958 --> 00:04:39,151
on.

72
00:04:40,716 --> 00:04:46,058
In March 2012, he reached 7th
place on the Forbes ranking, with

73
00:04:46,058 --> 00:04:47,076
$30 billion.

74
00:04:48,051 --> 00:04:55,771
Slim was still number 1, with $69
billion. The gap: $39 billion.

75
00:04:57,471 --> 00:05:02,103
That same month, an Abu Dhabi
fund, Mubadala, invested $2

76
00:05:02,103 --> 00:05:07,305
billion for a 5.63% stake in
Eike's group. Based on the deal,
as

77
00:05:07,305 --> 00:05:11,856
announced by the group, the empire
was worth about $35.5

78
00:05:11,856 --> 00:05:12,506
billion.

79
00:05:16,331 --> 00:05:20,271
Eike was the face of Brazil's
success story. He had bought the

80
00:05:20,271 --> 00:05:24,275
Hotel Glória, one of Rio's most
traditional hotels, to renovate

81
00:05:24,275 --> 00:05:28,151
it. He published a book, gave
talks, and appeared on magazine

82
00:05:28,151 --> 00:05:28,596
covers.

83
00:05:29,016 --> 00:05:32,857
But while the owner was shining,
the oil wasn't showing up the

84
00:05:32,857 --> 00:05:34,406
way it had been promised.

85
00:05:35,966 --> 00:05:39,001
Chapter 5. The well that didn't
gush.

86
00:05:40,036 --> 00:05:44,611
In early 2012, OGX finally started
producing at the Tubarão Azul

87
00:05:44,611 --> 00:05:46,541
field, in the Campos Basin.

88
00:05:47,866 --> 00:05:52,120
On the night of June 26, 2012, the
company released the number

89
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:56,443
the market was waiting for: each
well would produce about 5,000

90
00:05:56,443 --> 00:06:00,011
barrels a day. Far below what
analysts had imagined.

91
00:06:01,946 --> 00:06:10,471
The next day, the stock fell 25%,
from 8.37 reais to 6.25 reais.

92
00:06:11,586 --> 00:06:16,765
To calm investors, Eike made a
promise in October 2012: if OGX

93
00:06:16,765 --> 00:06:21,526
needed it, he himself would put up
to $1 billion into the

94
00:06:21,526 --> 00:06:24,951
company, buying new shares at 6.30
reais.

95
00:06:26,896 --> 00:06:31,944
It didn't help. In March 2013, the
new Forbes list showed Eike

96
00:06:31,944 --> 00:06:34,631
plunging from 7th to 100th place.

97
00:06:36,011 --> 00:06:41,128
And then came the final blow. On
July 1, 2013, OGX admitted that

98
00:06:41,128 --> 00:06:46,004
there was no technology available
to make three of its fields

99
00:06:46,004 --> 00:06:50,801
economically viable: Tubarão
Tigre, Tubarão Gato and Tubarão

100
00:06:50,801 --> 00:06:51,281
Areia.

101
00:06:52,696 --> 00:06:57,713
On July 3, the stock closed at
0.39 reais. More than 98% below

102
00:06:57,713 --> 00:07:01,031
its peak. And it would fall even
further.

103
00:07:02,066 --> 00:07:07,866
By Bloomberg's count, Eike's
fortune had reached $34.5 billion

104
00:07:07,866 --> 00:07:13,198
in March 2012. By July 2013, the
estimate was around $200

105
00:07:13,198 --> 00:07:13,946
million.

106
00:07:16,686 --> 00:07:20,987
In September, OGX called on Eike
to deliver the promised $1

107
00:07:20,987 --> 00:07:25,580
billion. Eike disputed the demand,
and the money never came. In

108
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:29,444
2014, with the company already in
reorganization, the

109
00:07:29,444 --> 00:07:33,526
independent directors released him
from that obligation.

110
00:07:33,946 --> 00:07:38,036
On October 30, 2013, OGX filed for
court-supervised

111
00:07:38,036 --> 00:07:42,606
reorganization, Brazil's version
of Chapter 11, with 11.2

112
00:07:42,606 --> 00:07:47,337
billion reais in debt. At the
time, it was described as the

113
00:07:47,337 --> 00:07:51,106
largest reorganization filing in
Latin America.

114
00:07:51,526 --> 00:07:57,502
And, in 2014, came that statement:
a negative net worth of $1

115
00:07:57,502 --> 00:07:58,286
billion.

116
00:07:59,626 --> 00:08:02,161
Chapter 6. The domino effect.

117
00:08:03,561 --> 00:08:07,091
The fall of OGX undermined
confidence in the whole group.

118
00:08:07,916 --> 00:08:12,459
The X companies depended on each
other. OSX, for example, built

119
00:08:12,459 --> 00:08:17,001
and leased oil platforms, and its
main customer was OGX itself.

120
00:08:19,016 --> 00:08:22,931
Creditors started collecting.
Mubadala, which had put in $2

121
00:08:22,931 --> 00:08:26,781
billion, began receiving payment
in assets, such as a gold

122
00:08:26,781 --> 00:08:27,776
mining company.

123
00:08:29,226 --> 00:08:32,156
And the story got a chapter that
looks like a movie script.

124
00:08:33,609 --> 00:08:37,805
In 2015, the courts seized Eike's
assets, including luxury cars.

125
00:08:37,805 --> 00:08:41,871
Days later, the judge in charge of
the case was caught driving

126
00:08:41,871 --> 00:08:45,936
the seized Porsche Cayenne through
the streets of Rio. He said

127
00:08:45,936 --> 00:08:50,001
he had kept the car in his
building for safety. He was
removed

128
00:08:50,001 --> 00:08:54,001
from Eike's cases and was later
convicted of misappropriating

129
00:08:54,001 --> 00:08:54,919
seized assets.

130
00:08:57,656 --> 00:09:01,541
Chapter 7. From magazine covers to
a prison cell.

131
00:09:02,491 --> 00:09:07,538
In January 2017, Operation
Eficiência, an offshoot of the Car

132
00:09:07,538 --> 00:09:10,931
Wash investigation in Rio,
targeted Eike.

133
00:09:11,351 --> 00:09:15,585
Federal prosecutors accused him of
paying $16.5 million in

134
00:09:15,585 --> 00:09:19,965
bribes to then-governor Sérgio
Cabral, through an account in

135
00:09:19,965 --> 00:09:20,476
Panama.

136
00:09:22,596 --> 00:09:27,652
Eike was in New York. On January
30, 2017, he landed in Rio and

137
00:09:27,652 --> 00:09:29,899
was arrested at the airport.

138
00:09:30,836 --> 00:09:34,775
The man who had once been the
richest in Brazil was taken to the

139
00:09:34,775 --> 00:09:36,068
Bangu prison complex.

140
00:09:36,816 --> 00:09:40,920
He spent about 3 months in Bangu,
until Justice Gilmar Mendes,

141
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:45,157
of Brazil's Supreme Court, granted
a habeas corpus that replaced

142
00:09:45,157 --> 00:09:47,871
his pretrial detention with house
arrest.

143
00:09:48,291 --> 00:09:52,749
In July 2018, a trial court
sentenced him to 30 years in
prison

144
00:09:52,749 --> 00:09:56,641
for bribery and money laundering.
The defense appealed.

145
00:09:59,151 --> 00:10:03,380
In November 2020, Justice Rosa
Weber, of the Supreme Court,

146
00:10:03,380 --> 00:10:07,752
approved the cooperation
agreement, a kind of plea deal,
Eike

147
00:10:07,752 --> 00:10:12,268
signed with the Prosecutor
General's Office, with a fine of
800

148
00:10:12,268 --> 00:10:13,271
million reais.

149
00:10:13,691 --> 00:10:18,185
Between 2019 and 2021, federal
trial courts in Rio also

150
00:10:18,185 --> 00:10:22,760
convicted him of insider trading
and market manipulation

151
00:10:22,760 --> 00:10:27,989
involving OGX and OSX shares. The
heaviest sentence, in February

152
00:10:27,989 --> 00:10:32,402
2021, was 11 years and 8 months.
These are trial court

153
00:10:32,402 --> 00:10:34,771
decisions, subject to appeal.

154
00:10:39,991 --> 00:10:42,821
Chapter 8. What was left of the X.

155
00:10:43,941 --> 00:10:45,331
Here's the final irony.

156
00:10:46,281 --> 00:10:49,691
Many of Eike's projects survived.
Just without him.

157
00:10:50,436 --> 00:10:54,393
MPX, the energy company, passed
into the hands of Germany's

158
00:10:54,393 --> 00:10:58,350
E.ON, changed its name to Eneva,
and is still listed on the

159
00:10:58,350 --> 00:10:59,356
stock exchange.

160
00:10:59,776 --> 00:11:04,309
LLX became Prumo, controlled by
the American fund EIG. And the

161
00:11:04,309 --> 00:11:08,915
Port of Açu, in the north of Rio
de Janeiro state, Eike's great

162
00:11:08,915 --> 00:11:13,083
dream, now operates as one of the
largest port and energy

163
00:11:13,083 --> 00:11:14,911
complexes in the country.

164
00:11:15,331 --> 00:11:19,289
The ideas had value. The problem
was the size of the promise and

165
00:11:19,289 --> 00:11:21,206
the speed at which it was sold.

166
00:11:22,466 --> 00:11:26,335
In interviews, Eike has stated
that he tried to create wealth

167
00:11:26,335 --> 00:11:30,395
for the country. Today, he lives
in Rio, far from the top of the

168
00:11:30,395 --> 00:11:33,186
rankings, and keeps announcing new
projects.

169
00:11:34,206 --> 00:11:38,009
The story of Eike Batista shows
something the market forgets

170
00:11:38,009 --> 00:11:41,811
from time to time: market value is
not money in your pocket.

171
00:11:43,446 --> 00:11:47,239
A company can be worth billions on
the stock exchange screen and

172
00:11:47,239 --> 00:11:50,261
have nothing to deliver from the
bottom of the sea.

173
00:11:50,681 --> 00:11:54,731
The X promised to multiply. And it
did. Mostly the debt.

174
00:11:56,401 --> 00:12:00,226
If you enjoyed this story,
subscribe to Fatos de Fortuna and

175
00:12:00,226 --> 00:12:04,242
tell us in the comments: which
rise and fall do you want to see

176
00:12:04,242 --> 00:12:04,561
next?
